  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "District Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71980649e42d-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 49,
              "start": 49
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The district court granted a stay of execution on February 17, 2000."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner argues that the Sixth Circuit exceeded its authority by withdrawing its judgment affirming the denial of habeas corpus relief six months after the Supreme Court denied certiorari, affecting the stay."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 9,
              "start": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner contends that Rule 41(b) does not permit extending the time for issuing a mandate beyond the seven\u2011day period after a rehearing petition is resolved."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the Sixth Circuit exceeded its authority by withdrawing its judgment affirming the denial of habeas corpus relief six months after the Supreme Court denied certiorari."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, rule 41(b) specifically deals with the seven\u2011day period for issuance following the expiration of the time for a petition for rehearing."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 9,
                "start": 9
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, rule 41 does not allow any other circumstances."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 12,
                "start": 12
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, all the record shows that the mandate did not issue."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Smith",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71980649e42d-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 52,
                "start": 52
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Smith, the State did not need the mandate in order to proceed; a mandate merely directs the district court what to do next and is independent of the merits."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. SMITH",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71980649e42d-0003-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 53,
                "start": 53
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. SMITH, the stay of execution dissolved by operation of law when the appeal was disposed of upon the affirmance of the denial of rehearing."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71980649e42d-0001-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 23,
                "start": 23
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, additional mitigating circumstances do not undermine the three aggravating circumstances nor rise to the level of innocence of the death penalty."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71980649e42d-0001-0008"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 36,
                "start": 36
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, the Fourth, Fifth, and Sixth Circuits, including the decision below, hold that the ultimate decision of when to issue the mandate lies within the broad discretion of the court of appeals."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Shors",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71980649e42d-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 49,
                "start": 49
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Shors, a court of appeals decision is not final until it issues its mandate; until then the case remains pending."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondent Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    }
